ing to adopt some of its pieces of advice as many as possible. In November, I started to learning Java seriously.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--2-1xRawN--/f_auto/v1722860399/public/Placeholder%2011","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2021-01-04T17:09:00.000Z"},{"id":"7g0HgLJUC","title":"Perl Weekly Challenge 93: Max Points and Sum Path","url":"http://blogs.perl.org/users/laurent_r/2021/01/perl-weekly-challenge-93-max-points-and-sum-path.html","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/perl-weekly-challenge-93-max-points-and-sum-path-7g0hgljuc","summary":"Week 93 of the Perl Weekly Challenge is over. This blog post offers some solutions to this challenge. Please don\u2019t read on if you intend to complete the challenge on your own.Task 1: Max Points. You are given set of co-ordinates @N . Write a script to count maximum points on a straight line.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--1KxV4ohY--/f_auto/v1722860400/public/Placeholder%2007","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2021-01-02T21:33:00.000Z"},{"id":"Otj-UYACN","title":"Annual Report - 2020","url":"http://blogs.perl.org/users/mohammad_s_anwar/2021/01/annual-report---2020.html","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/annual-report---2020-otj-uyacn","summary":"Perl Weekly Challenge is celebrating its 10th anniversary this year. Team PWC members share their thoughts on the year that was. PWC will continue to run the challenge in 2020 and 2021 as well. This is PWC's overall annual report for the year 2020. For more information on the Weekly Challenge, visit the Perl Weekly Challenge website.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--0_ODbtD2--/f_auto/v1722860399/public/Placeholder%2008","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2021-01-01T11:37:00.000Z"},{"id":"S2YI50WpG","title":"From a Reflection on The Weekly Challenge 092 Task 1","url":"http://blogs.perl.org/users/c_y_fung/2021/01/from-a-reflection-on-the-weekly-challenge-092-task-1.html","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/from-a-reflection-on-the-weekly-challenge-092-task-1-s2yi50wpg","summary":"The Weekly Challenge #092 Task: Isomorphic Strings. Write a script to check if the given strings are Isomorphic. Print 1 if they are otherwise 0. See the comment section. Update: Ben Bullock has provided script for my question. Thanks Ben.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--2-1xRawN--/f_auto/v1722860399/public/Placeholder%2011","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2021-01-01T03:09:00.000Z"},{"id":"2jzT-uL5a","title":"I'm Making Headway Now","url":"http://blogs.perl.org/users/ben_bullock/2020/12/im-making-headway-now.html","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/i-m-making-headway-now-2jzt-ul5a","summary":"A post on reddit claimed that my module JSON::Parse was not only failing some of the JSON Test Suite tests, but also crashing on one of them. I found that after 80,000 open brackets the stack was overflowing, causing the crash to occur. If I added a printf in the midst of my code the printf would cause the stack overflow, so it wasn't actually due to my code.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--OHB84bZF--/f_auto/v1722860399/public/Placeholder%2010","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2020-12-30T18:54:00.000Z"},{"id":"Xwg_fn1YR","title":"Perl weekly challenge 093","url":"http://blogs.perl.org/users/joan_mimosinnet/2020/12/perl-weekly-challenge-093.html","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/perl-weekly-challenge-093-xwg-fn1yr","summary":"This is a Raku answer for the 093 Perl Weekly Challenge. This is also my first post. The solution looks at points with equal slope to see if they are in a straight line. The binary tree has been defined as 'lines of nodes', with 0 if the node is empty. The representation of the tree is: 1 2 3 4 0 5 6.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--0_ODbtD2--/f_auto/v1722860399/public/Placeholder%2008","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2020-12-30T15:36:00.000Z"},{"id":"6jvlgQqP8","title":"Perl weekly challenge 93","url":"http://blogs.perl.org/users/james_curtis-smith/2020/12/perl-weekly-challenge-93.html","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/perl-weekly-challenge-93-6jvlgqqp8","summary":"Week 93 of the Perl Weekly Challenge organized by Mohammad S. Anwar. This weekly challenge deadline is due in a few days (January 3, 2021) This blog post offers some solutions to this challenge, please don\u2019t read on if you intend to complete the challenge on your own.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--1KxV4ohY--/f_auto/v1722860400/public/Placeholder%2007","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2020-12-28T12:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"82u-92BRC","title":"Perl Weekly Challenge 92: Isomorphic Strings and Insert Intervals","url":"http://blogs.perl.org/users/laurent_r/2020/12/perl-weekly-challenge-92-isomorphic-strings-and-insert-intervals.html","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/perl-weekly-challenge-92-isomorphic-strings-and-insert-intervals-82u-92brc","summary":"This week's challenge is Week 92 of the Perl Weekly Challenge. This blog post offers some solutions to this challenge. Please don\u2019t read on if you intend to complete the challenge on your own. We\u2019re using 5 test cases. For each string pair, the program calls the is-isomorphic subroutine, which does the bulk of the work.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--58gMhC4P--/f_auto/v1722860399/public/Placeholder%2012","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2020-12-27T17:36:00.000Z"},{"id":"06DumGS1Y","title":"Misusing newSVpv","url":"http://blogs.perl.org/users/ben_bullock/2020/12/misusing-newsvpv.html","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/misusing-newsvpv-06dumgs1y","summary":"I managed to cause another set of obscure bugs by misusing newSVpv. The goal of this code is to split the RGB and the alpha (transparent) part of a PNG image. It causes the crash on Solaris and other operating systems because the above statement is a bad idea. What happens is that Perl copies \"len\" bytes from my string.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--ZrL_HSsR--/f_auto/v1722860399/public/Placeholder%2006","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2020-12-26T14:26:00.000Z"},{"id":"iHfk8dP7T","title":"Amazon.com/mytv Launching Monthly Subscription Options For Prime Video - Movies & Tv","url":"http://blogs.perl.org/users/_robertredford/2020/12/amazoncommytv-launching-monthly-subscription-options-for-prime-video---movies-tv.html","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/amazon-com-mytv-launching-monthly-subscription-options-for-prime-video---movies-tv-ihfk8dp7t","summary":null,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--CxzD6vbw--/f_auto/v1722860399/public/Placeholder%2005","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2020-12-24T11:20:00.000Z"}],"similar_handles":["scottlowe","rails","beamrad","twitter","fbr"],"opposite_handles":["alexfinn","tbpn","kloss_xyz","ryolu_","felixrieseberg"],"similar":[{"id":"scottlowe","handle":"scottlowe","name":"Scott's Weblog","is_squad":false,"x":-4.822,"y":-3.4668,"cluster_id":1,"posts_collected":61,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/t_logo,f_auto/v1/logos/5d8530c407894ba5b9b8ab602c57f10d","features_preview":{"posts_per_week":0.391591,"median_upvotes":0.0,"author_present_share":0.0,"hype_score":0.0,"avg_read_time":3.901639,"tag_diversity":0.786885},"top_tags_preview":[["cloud",29],["networking",28],["security",23]],"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[0.8088,6.2206],"cadence_depth":[-3.1471,-4.8676],"hype_variety":[-5.3676,-0.1618],"title_style":[-0.1176,-2.4559]}},{"id":"rails","handle":"rails","name":"Rails","is_squad":false,"x":-5.086,"y":-3.2804,"cluster_id":1,"posts_collected":300,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/t_logo,f_auto/v1/logos/d44501fa43a2441a9e27a08367cdfa52","features_preview":{"posts_per_week":1.432896,"median_upvotes":1.0,"auth